<h2>Is Cubii as Good as Walking?</h2>
<p>No, and it does not need to be. Walking burns more per minute, works more muscles, and is weight bearing, which matters for bone health. The advantage of a Cubii is that you can use it while doing something else, for far longer than you would walk on a workday.</p>
<p>The best approach is both: walk when you can, and pedal when you are stuck at the desk. Our full comparison, <a href="/is-under-desk-elliptical-as-good-as-walking/">is an under desk elliptical as good as walking</a>, breaks down the numbers.</p>

<h2>Cubii Weight Loss: What Is Realistic?</h2>
<p>A Cubii can contribute to weight loss, but it will not drive it alone. At light effort, most people burn roughly 100 to 150 calories per hour of pedaling. Spread two hours across a workday and you might add 200 to 300 calories, which is meaningful over weeks if your diet stays the same.</p>
<p>The trap is eating those calories back. Owners who report weight loss usually combine daily pedaling with diet changes and other exercise. Read <a href="/can-you-lose-weight-with-under-desk-elliptical/">can you lose weight with an under desk elliptical</a> for a realistic plan.</p>

<h2>Which Cubii Under Desk Elliptical to Use Daily</h2>
<p>For everyday use under one desk, the JR2 is the one to get. It is heavier than the budget models, which keeps it planted and smooth. If app tracking will keep you motivated, the JR2+ adds Bluetooth.</p>
